# p_b2e9 — Marco's Minimal Commute: Scarf, Umbrella, and Lunchbox Stay Home

The evidence is unambiguous: Marco does not take his scarf or umbrella to work. Every document that placed `class:scarf` or `class:umbrella` at OUT_OF_HOUSE during his 14:00–23:00 shift has failed (0.14 on 3 sightings each), while the same classes at `entry_hook_e1` and `entry_floor_e1` have held at 0.93–0.97. Marco apparently dresses for the weather in the morning, leaves his outerwear at the entry, and goes to work in a jacket or light layer. The scarf and umbrella remain at the entry all day.

Similarly, Marco's lunchbox is not in the cupboard during his shift (10 empty looks) and not out of the house (2 in-house sightings). The most parsimonious explanation: he packs his lunch on the counter in the morning, and on days when he doesn't take it (or after he's grabbed it and the robot sees the next day's box already packed) it sits on the counter. This document places the lunchbox at `counter_k1` during 14:00–22:00 on weekdays.

Marco's journal and vitamins also stay in the house during his shift (2 in-house sightings each, 3–5 empty looks at their resting spots). He journals in the early morning and evening, not at work. The vitamins sit on the counter or in the medicine cabinet, not in his work bag.

This document differs from p_a3f1 (lunchbox in cupboard) and p_b7c2 (lunchbox, journal, vitamins all out of house) by keeping all of Marco's personal items in the house during his work shift. It also corrects the scarf/umbrella error shared by p_a1b2, p_e5f6, p_7890, and p_c3d4.

What would refute this: if the robot finds Marco's scarf at the entry hook empty during 14:00–22:00 on a weekday (meaning he took it), or finds the lunchbox in the cupboard at 18:00, the model is wrong.

