# p_8c3d — Dog Dinner at the Floor, Guitar on the Couch After Nine

The dog food bag tells a simple story: it rests on the pantry shelf during the day, but at dinner time (roughly 19:00) Yuki brings it out to the kitchen floor to feed the dog. The 20:00 and 22:00 passes both find it on `floor_k_k1`, while the 18:00 pass finds it at `pantry_shelf_k1`. The mixture's worst-object list confirms this: it predicted the pantry shelf at 20:00 and was wrong twice. The bag stays on the floor through the evening (the dog's bowl is also on the kitchen floor, so the bag is set down next to it).

The guitar follows a quieter pattern: it rests on the bedroom floor through the day (Yuki practices in the afternoon, 15:00–16:30, per p_a3f1's claim which has not been contradicted). But at 22:00 the pass finds it on the couch in the living room, where Yuki was also seen at 18:00 and 22:00. This suggests Yuki brings the guitar to the couch for a relaxed evening session after dinner, once the kitchen is cleared. The bedroom floor is the daytime resting spot; the couch is the post-dinner playing spot.

This document is narrow and specific: it only makes claims about the dog food bag's evening location and the guitar's post-22:00 location. It does not attempt to model the full cooking cycle (p_f4a7 does that) or Marco's commute (p_b2e9 does that).

What would refute this: if the dog food bag is found on the pantry shelf at 20:00 or 22:00 on a weekday, or if the guitar is found on the bedroom floor at 22:00 on a weekday.

